  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "Written in **ascending order**, the solutions to $|1-y|=8$ are $y=${{field-1}} and $y=$\n{{field-2}}.",
  "worked_solution": "Either the positive or negative of the expression inside the absolute value must be equal to the right-hand side of the equation.\n\nSo, we set up the two corresponding equations and solve them independently:\n\n- If $|1-y|=1-y,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|1-y| & =8 \\\\ 1-y & =8 \\\\ -y & =7 \\\\ y & =-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|1-y|=-(1-y),$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|1-y| & =8 \\\\ -(1-y) & =8 \\\\ -1+y & =8 \\\\ y & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $y=-7$ and $y=9.$",
